What this means in plain words (not part of the legal terms above)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Allowed:
  - Using the components in your own personal or commercial websites and
    apps, including closed-source and paid products.
  - Changing the components however you like.

Required:
  - A visible credit with a link to Relic UI somewhere in your project.
  - Keeping the credit comment and copyright notice in the source files.

Not allowed:
  - Selling, sublicensing or redistributing the components themselves, alone
    or in a bundle, including versions ported to other frameworks.
  - Publishing them as part of a competing component library, UI kit or
    template marketplace.
  - Using the Relic UI name or logo for your own project. The license covers
    the code only.
